issue.body:
I am running MAVSDK v.0.42.0 on Ubuntu 20.04 inside a ROS2 node. Sometimes the node dies right after I initialize MAVSDK. The error however occurs non deterministic with a 1/20 chance. (I just started it over and over again and sometimes it crashes)
After a lot of try and error debugging, I noticed that it happens every time `set_rate_battery` fails. I couldn't figure out why it fails but every time it does I get the error `Promise already satisfied`.


```
[my-node-1] [INFO] [1630672509.497487560] [uuid63085.my_node_node]: Setting rate of battery failed
[my-node-1] terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::future_error'
[my-node-1]   what():  std::future_error: Promise already satisfied
[ERROR] [my-node-1]: process has died [pid 145033, exit code -6, cmd '/home/user/my-project/install/my_node/lib/my_node/my_node --ros-args -r __node:=my_node_node -r __ns:=/uuid63085 --params-file /tmp/launch_params_vzif_yms'].
```

```C++
mavsdk_check_result_telemetry(telemetry_->set_rate_battery(2.0), "battery");
telemetry_->subscribe_battery([this](mavsdk::Telemetry::Battery battery) {
    auto msg = std_msgs::msg::Float32();
    msg.data = battery.remaining_percent;
    pub_state_battery_->publish(msg);
});
```
```C++
void MyClass::mavsdk_check_result_telemetry(mavsdk::Telemetry::Result result, string type)
{
    if (result != mavsdk::Telemetry::Result::Success) {
        RCLCPP_INFO(this->get_logger(), "%s", ("Setting rate of " + type + " failed").c_str());
    } else {
        RCLCPP_INFO(this->get_logger(), "%s", ("Setting rate of " + type + " succeeded").c_str());
    }
}
```

